# Phrases that must never appear in a *city pack comment*, base64-encoded.
#
# Distinct from trip-patterns.b64, and the distinction matters. Those are
# literal fragments of an instance — a date, a party size — and are forbidden
# everywhere. These are ordinary domain vocabulary: prose in AGENTS.md, in the
# specs, and in this very toolchain has to talk about a stay window in order to
# forbid it. Applying them globally produced ten false positives on the first
# run and would have taught the next contributor to bypass the gate.
#
# A pack describes a city. The moment one of its comments ties that city to
# somebody's stay, the calendar stops being a public fact and becomes a
# signature.

c3RheSB3aW5kb3c=
b3VyIHN0YXk=
dGhlIHRyaXAgd2luZG93
ZmVuw6p0cmUgZGUgc8Opam91cg==
bm90cmUgc8Opam91cg==
